# Input to the benchmark lock. `make lock` compiles this into requirements-bench.txt, pinned and
# hashed like the runtime lock. OR-Tools is a benchmark-only dependency (docs/design.md 8.3): this
# file is installed for development and CI, and never by the production image.
#
# carpool-domain is listed for the same reason requirements.in lists it: so the resolver reads it
# from the working tree rather than looking for it on PyPI.
#
# Constrained by the runtime lock, so the two can be installed into one environment without either
# moving a package the other pinned.
-c requirements.txt
-e ./packages/domain
-e ./packages/bench
